-; CME MDP3 Market Data Configuration
-;
-; cme_cpus -- optional. Comma list of EXACTLY 5 cpu ids, in actor order:
-;
-;     recovery, message_processor, msg_buf_a, socket_proc_a, socket_proc_b
-;
-; Absent or empty => no pinning at all, which is what this file did before the
-; key existed and what the production recorder wants. A list of any other
-; length is a startup error, not a partial application.
-;
-; Layout below is NUMA node 2 (cpus 16-23,48-55). That node measured 13.4%
-; total busy over 12 s while nodes 0/1/3 ran 105-152%. It is NOT the NIC-local
-; node -- ens1f0/ens1f1 are both numa_node=0 -- and that is deliberate: the
-; probe's measurement window starts at the socket read, so the NIC-to-cpu
-; hop is outside what we are measuring. Quiet beats close here.
-;
-; Nothing on this box is isolated (isolcpus, nohz_full and rcu_nocbs are all
-; empty in /proc/cmdline), so these cpus are quiet, not reserved. The kernel
-; can and will schedule other work on them.
-;
-; SMT siblings are (N, N+32): cpu16 and cpu48 are one physical core. sock_a
-; and sock_b of one channel are busy on the same packets at the same instant,
-; so they are kept on different physical cores throughout.
-;
-; Resulting physical core map:
-;   phys16: 16 ES sock_a  | 48 ZN sock_a
-;   phys17: 17 ES msgproc | 49 ES msgbuf
-;   phys18: 18 ES sock_b  | 50 ZN msgproc
-;   phys19: 19 TachBook   | 51 all three recovery actors
-;   phys20: 20 NQ sock_a  | 52 ZN sock_b
-;   phys21: 21 NQ msgproc | 53 NQ msgbuf
-;   phys22: 22 NQ sock_b  | 54 ZN msgbuf
-;   phys23: 23 TachBook   | 55 TachBook
-;
-; The three recovery actors share cpu51 on the assumption that recovery is
-; idle once the books are built. That assumption is only true after startup.
-; During the first minutes all three replay snapshots on one cpu, which is
-; one more reason the first 5 minutes of a run are not measurement data.
-;
-; TachBook cpus (19,23,55) are set separately, in the kaspr ini.
